GitHub Actions was used to prepare the CI/CD workflow and automate the application deployment process.

The workflow is designed to:

Trigger automatically when code is pushed to the configured GitHub branch.
Install project dependencies.
Build the application.
Run tests when available.
Deploy the generated build to the target Azure service.
Frontend CI/CD Flow
GitHub Repository
       ↓
GitHub Actions
       ↓
npm install
       ↓
npm run build
       ↓
dist/
       ↓
Azure Static Web Apps
Backend CI/CD Flow
GitHub Repository
       ↓
GitHub Actions
       ↓
Restore Dependencies
       ↓
Build .NET Application
       ↓
Publish
       ↓
Azure App Service

This provides an automated deployment workflow between GitHub and Microsoft Azure, reducing the need for manual deployments after code changes.
